Headlines
================================================================================
1. ARCHITECTURE WORKS. Seq and par MALA chains agree end-to-end at every
   K_MALA tested (16..512). Both arrive at the same final phi. The
   compositional parallel-MALA o parallel-PF wiring is correct.

2. PARALLEL BIF: closed-form stationary J* + associative-scan h matches
   the serial BIF to ZERO error -- the closed-form Riccati fixed point
   IS the exact stationary BIF for LGSSM, and the affine h recurrence
   composes exactly via the (a,b) o (a',b') = (a'a, a'b + b') rule.

3. WINDOWED MALA: iters/K drops from 0.63 (small K) to 0.46 (large K),
   sub-linear scaling. The flat un-windowed sweep was 0.30 * K (linear)
   so windowing IS slowing iter growth, but not enough to flatten to O(1).

4. NO SPEEDUP CROSSOVER at the inner-PF sizes tested. Speedup hovers
   at 0.3-0.4x across K_MALA = 16..512. Per-iter parallel cost is one
   vmap-50 PF; on this LGSSM at T=1024, N=32 that costs ~5x a single
   PF, so even iters/K ~ 0.5 doesn't beat sequential.

   For speedup the inner PF needs to be substantially heavier (larger
   T or N) so that the vmap-50 amortisation pays off. This is a
   sweep-the-inner-PF question, not an architectural one.
